{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VFLez9aQ2LqgfYrpxwLsRi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-12-2245-parallelize-round0-cpu-postprocess\n2\t\n3\tRound 0 constraint evaluation at APC 300 spends ~200ms of its 662ms total on serial CPU post-processing (transpose + iDFT + polynomial construction), executed once per AIR × 3 calls inside a sequential loop over 623 AIRs. This work is embarrassingly parallel — each AIR's post-processing is independent. Restructuring the loop to collect raw GPU results first, then batch-process them with rayon's `par_iter` across 32 cores, should reduce this CPU overhead from ~200ms to ~7-13ms, yielding an estimated 28% improvement on Round 0 and 7-8% on STARK excl trace.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f2fc226-1649-44e7-a922-02ccd916e4bc","uuid":"1b0cbf5f-388f-4f4a-8547-96387bb34599","timestamp":"2026-04-12T20:23:38.518Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-12-2245-parallelize-round0-cpu-postprocess\n\nRound 0 constraint evaluation at APC 300 spends ~200ms of its 662ms total on serial CPU post-processing (transpose + iDFT + polynomial construction), executed once per AIR × 3 calls inside a sequential loop over 623 AIRs. This work is embarrassingly parallel — each AIR's post-processing is independent. Restructuring the loop to collect raw GPU results first, then batch-process them with rayon's `par_iter` across 32 cores, should reduce this CPU overhead from ~200ms to ~7-13ms, yielding an estimated 28% improvement on Round 0 and 7-8% on STARK excl trace.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
