ows' results on the GPU in separate slots and do a single D2H transfer at the end, then sum everything on the CPU. This requires allocating a larger GPU buffer to hold all window results simultaneously and restructuring the kernel launches to fill these slots before pulling everything back in one go.\n\nLooking at how the results are actually used, I see the code just sums all the per-window evaluations together, which means there's real potential to either move that summation to the GPU or at least batch the data transfers more efficiently.\n\nThe key optimization I'm seeing is to accumulate all windows into a single GPU buffer using atomic operations rather than copying results back after each window. This would reduce the D2H transfers from N_GROUPS down to just one per round, and we could also batch multiple degenerate windows into fewer kernel launches to cut down on launch overhead. generate kernel and regular kernel both write to d_accum. The fill_zero + kernel launch + to_host pattern suggests they each produce independent partial sums that get summed on CPU. If instead we don't zero the accumulator between windows and let each kernel ADD to it, we get the sum directly on the GPU.\n\nLooking at the kernel code, they likely use atomicAdd to accumulate. If they already use atomics, then we can just skip the per-window fill_zero + to_host and let everything accumulate into one buffer. The fill_zero at line 844-846 zeros the accumulator before each window, and the kernels write results via atomicAdd with u64 accumulators to avoid overflow in modular arithmetic.\n\nIf we remove the per-window fill_zero and let all windows accumulate into the same buffer, we'd get the sum directly—just one fill_zero and one to_host per round instead of N_GROUPS. The tricky part is that the degenerate kernel path also does an H2D copy of eq_ub_slice, so if windows have different eq_ub data, we'd need to batch that too. Let me check the CUDA kernel code to verify the atomic accumulation pattern.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3717,"cache_read_input_tokens":68848,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3717},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f2fc226-1649-44e7-a922-02ccd916e4bc","uuid":"e3d1e12c-b0cf-486d-9239-342b225e9c5c"}
