{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0177zVf6TUzmixBBczm5t5ue","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-12-2330-batch-stacked-reduction-mle-sync\n2\t\n3\tThe stacked reduction MLE rounds in `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval()` perform a synchronous D2H copy (`to_host()` with full GPU pipeline drain) per height group per round. With ~400+ height groups and 17 MLE rounds, this creates ~7,000+ pipeline-draining sync points per segment. Since both the regular and degenerate CUDA kernels already use atomic accumulation into a shared `d_accum` buffer, and the final result is a sum across all windows, these per-window syncs are unnecessary — a single `fill_zero` + `to_host` per round suffices. This eliminates the dominant source of CPU-GPU synchronization overhead, which profiling shows accounts for the majority of the 287ms MLE rounds time at APC 300 (vs ~60ms of actual GPU kernel time).\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01SZdKKsqd7fenKWAYHkBtU3","session_id":"3f2fc226-1649-44e7-a922-02ccd916e4bc","uuid":"aaa6479a-22b6-49e2-848b-de4e076f04db","timestamp":"2026-04-12T20:46:06.179Z"}
